/* book exam traps: Reversing the ISFET sign. For an n-channel device at a fixed gate bias the output falls as pH rises, because the threshold voltage rises and the overdrive shrinks. | Forgetting the 2 electrons per glucose molecule, or using the moles of glucose directly in Q = nF. The factor of two comes from H₂O₂ oxidation at platinum. | Calling a bare ISFET a biosensor. It is a pH sensor until an enzyme or antibody layer makes it an EnFET or an IMFET. */
